li-7-p2 = prose (cons "- Girard: desire itself is learned by imitation. Imitation converges many on the same objects; rivalry follows; when tension grows, an arbitrary victim is blamed and expelled in collective murder, and culture forms around it." (cons "- Tarde, The Laws of Imitation (1890): a sociology founded on imitation." (cons "- The neurotypical mind resolves to social baselines as a continuity mechanism of the superorganism; where rational cognition threatens a bounded group's self-boundary, boundary preservation suppresses rational expression. Judging a whole human from one action is a model effective at producing mass death; respect comes with agency and responsibility, person by person, in each one's relational world." nil)))
